From: Shivam Rawat <shivrawa@qti.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: Fix stale rpmh votes after suspend

Backport of upstream commit d9108bfdb746 (torvalds/linux; Fixes: f248d5d5159a
"drm/msm/a6xx: Fix PDC sleep sequence"; Tested-by Neil Armstrong on SM8650-HDK).
Patchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/730652/
Message-ID: <20260605-assorted-fixes-june-v1-1-2caa04f7287c@oss.qualcomm.com>

The GMU_STATUS_FW_START check in a6xx_rpmh_stop() is inverted: once the GMU
firmware has run, the GPU RSC is never put to sleep and its RPMh BCM/ARC votes
stay active through system suspend. On X1E that kept AOP out of CXSD and DDR
low power. On the Thor it matches DDR held at 1555 MHz (4224 MHz after Eden)
across s2idle. Also halt the GMU CM3 core before stopping RPMh, as upstream.
---
diff --color -ru a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c	2026-10-14 20:21:09.512322302 +0300
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c	2026-10-14 20:21:09.519509693 +0300
@@ -655,7 +655,7 @@
 	int ret;
 	u32 val;
 
-	if (test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
+	if (!test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
 		return;
 
 	if (adreno_is_a840(adreno_gpu))
@@ -1481,6 +1481,9 @@
 	/* Stop the interrupts and mask the hardware */
 	a6xx_gmu_irq_disable(gmu);
 
+	/* Halt the gmu cm3 core */
+	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_CM3_SYSRESET, 1);
+
 	/* Tell RPMh to power off the GPU */
 	a6xx_rpmh_stop(gmu);
 
